			"Message": "chore(Monorepo): Synchronize all elements with build tooling and optimizations\n\nThis commit advances all submodules to their latest commits, introducing major build tooling capabilities, code quality improvements, and production optimizations across the Land ecosystem.\n\n## Build Tooling & Compiler Updates\n\n### Rest: OXC Migration & Phase 3 Features\n- **Compiler Migration**: Replaced SWC with OXC (Oxidation Compiler) for 10-100x faster TypeScript compilation\n- **Phase 3 Features**: Added Bundle system, NLS processing, Worker compilation, and PrivateFieldTransform\n- **Compile Subcommand**: New standalone TypeScript compiler for outputting to specified directories\n- **NPM Packaging**: Full `@codeeditorland/rest` package with platform-specific binaries\n\n### Wind & Worker: Production Builds\n- **Wind**: Generated minified production build (removed source maps, tree-shaking)\n- **Worker**: Minified Service Worker artifacts (~10KB → ~2.6KB), removed .js.map files\n\n## Code Quality & Style\n\n### Formatting & Lint\n- **Cocoon**: Applied consistent code formatting (quotes, imports, spacing) across entire module\n- **Grove**: Standardized Rust formatting, doc comment indentation, import organization\n- **Mist**: Added clippy allow attributes (tabs_in_doc_comments, unnecessary_lazy_evaluations)\n\n### Naming Conventions (Grove NC-05)\n- Renamed transport modules to PascalCase: gRPCTransport.rs → GrpcTransport.rs, IPCTransport.rs → IpcTransport.rs\n- Verified namespace patterns, file naming, directory naming conventions\n\n## Bug Fixes\n\n### Air: Compilation Fixes\n- Added cfg guards for platform-specific methods in Daemon/Updates (Windows)\n- Removed unnecessary mut in Updates/CancelDownload\n- Fixed invalid await on non-future in Binary.rs shutdown code\n- Dropped unused JoinHandle results in Binary.rs startup\n\n### Mist: Attribute Cleanup\n- Removed redundant #[must_use] from start() (already applied via anyhow::Result)\n\n## Infrastructure\n\n### Mountain: Submodule Cleanup\n- Removed macOS/Mountain submodule (build handling consolidated in main Mountain via Library.rs)\n\nImpact: Brings OXC compiler performance to Rest, completes production build pipeline for Wind/Worker, resolves compilation issues in Air, and achieves code consistency across the monorepo.",
