			"Message": "chore(Monorepo): Synchronize multiple elements with TODO cleanup and implementation completion\n\nThis commit advances all major submodules to their latest commits, featuring significant implementation work across the Land ecosystem.\n\n## Implementation Completion\n\n### Air: Complete All TODOs\n- Implemented all 35 remaining TODOs in the Air daemon:\n  - Backup/restore for config and data directories\n  - Disk space check with platform-specific implementation\n  - Platform-specific installation stubs (Windows MSI, macOS, Linux AppImage/DEB/RPM)\n  - Telemetry sending (dev-build-only)\n  - Daemon integration (service management, gRPC status, config operations)\n  - Diagnostics, log tailing, state/connection dumps\n- Standardized remaining TODO comments to FUTURE naming convention\n\n### Mountain: Debug Infrastructure & Code Quality\n- Added `FeatureState::Debug::DebugState` module for debug provider registrations\n- Implemented TreeView badge support with validation\n- Consolidated binary entry point to `Source/Library.rs` for mobile/desktop parity\n- Thread safety: Replaced unsafe `static mut` with `RwLock` in `Scheme.rs`\n- Naming consistency: Renamed collections to singular form throughout\n- Added Git LFS configuration to exclude files exceeding 100MB limit\n\n### Wind & Cocoon: Import Optimization & Documentation\n- Removed 14 unused `Context` and `Effect` imports in Wind\n- Standardized TODO prefixes across modules:\n  - FUTURE: Planned enhancements\n  - DEPENDENCY: External library dependencies (Hickory DNS, Mountain backend)\n  - DEPRECATED: Confirmed for removal (Bridge.ts)\n  - SECURITY/PERFORMANCE/TESTING/DOCUMENTATION/LOGGING: Specialized concerns\n\n## Dependency Updates\n\n- **Mist**: Updated TODO to DEPENDENCY markers for Hickory DNS features\n- **Output**: Updated ESBuild TODO comments to FUTURE\n- **SideCar**: Refactored TODO to DEPENDENCY markers for Tauri 2.x features\n\nImpact: Completes Air implementation work, establishes debug infrastructure in Mountain, achieves documentation consistency across all TypeScript and Rust elements, and improves thread safety in the native backend.",
